com.automation.sites.listeners.AlterSuiteForCoverageMapListener
# ReportPortal's own TestNG agent (com.epam.reportportal:agent-java-testng —
# see pom.xml's dependency block). Registered here, not via @Listeners or a
# testng-suites/*.xml <listeners> entry, so it covers every suite (web,
# mobile, API) without having to touch 12+ suite XML files by hand — same
# reasoning as AlterSuiteForCoverageMapListener above. Safe to leave
# ServiceLoader-registered on every run: the agent reads rp.enable at
# startup (see reportportal.properties + pom.xml's reportportal.enable
# property, forwarded to the forked JVM the same way coverage.map.enabled
# is) and is a complete no-op — no network calls, nothing written anywhere —
# whenever that resolves to anything other than "true", which is the
# default. Only CI legs that explicitly pass -Dreportportal.enable=true
# (see github-ci.yml) actually report to a ReportPortal server.
com.epam.reportportal.testng.ReportPortalTestNGListener
